The fixed sky in internal/catalog/data comes from d3-celestial
(https://github.com/ofrohn/d3-celestial), BSD 3-Clause License,
Copyright (c) 2015, Olaf Frohn, built with scripts/catalog.py. Its sources:
- stars: XHIP, An Extended Hipparcos Compilation (Anderson & Francis 2012, VizieR V/137D)
- star names: the IAU list and the HD/HIP/Bayer/Flamsteed cross indexes (VizieR IV/27A, IV/22)
- constellation lines and names: the IAU constellation pages; borders: Davenhall & Leggett 1989 (VizieR VI/49)
- Messier objects: SEDS, H. Frommert (messier.seds.org)
- Milky Way outline: Jose R. Vieira (skymap.com)

Positions of the Sun, the Moon and the planets: Paul Schlyter, "How to compute
planetary positions" (stjarnhimlen.se); precession and eclipses after Jean Meeus,
"Astronomical Algorithms". Meteor shower figures: International Meteor Organization.
Cloud forecast: Open-Meteo.com (CC BY 4.0). Place names: © OpenStreetMap contributors.
Satellite positions: SGP4 written out in Go (internal/sat) after David Vallado's
reference code, "Revisiting Spacetrack Report #3" (Vallado, Crawford, Hujsak &
Kelso, AIAA 2006-6753), checked against its published test cases. Orbital
elements: CelesTrak (celestrak.org).
